---
import Layout from '@components/Layout.astro';
import ScoreBar from '@components/ScoreBar.astro';
---

<Layout title="About — How's Pot Doing?" current="about">
  <article class="about">
    <h1>About How's Pot Doing</h1>
    <h2>How the Legality of cannabis is calculated</h2>

    <p>We confirm legality on government sites, specifically <code>.gov</code> sites. We find the most plain language quote to determine legality. Then we calculate the percentage of legal gray area you're risking in that location.</p>
    <p>It's 80% legal for recreational, but only 30% when medical cannabis is the only option. Store purchase and home cultivation each add 10 points if allowed.</p>

    <ScoreBar
      label="80% for recreational legal, plus 10% for stores, plus 10% for home grow"
      segments={[
        { width: 80, color: '#2fae2f' },
        { width: 10, color: '#1f9a1f' },
        { width: 10, color: '#007a00' },
      ]}
      rows={[
        { points: '80%', label: 'Recreational legal' },
        { points: '+10%', label: 'Can buy in stores' },
        { points: '+10%', label: 'Can grow at home' },
      ]}
    />

    <p class="or">— or if recreational isn't legal —</p>

    <ScoreBar
      label="30% for medical only, plus 10% for patient stores, plus 10% for patient home grow"
      segments={[
        { width: 30, color: '#fee03c' },
        { width: 10, color: '#f0d21e' },
        { width: 10, color: '#e5c400' },
      ]}
      rows={[
        { points: '30%', label: 'Medical only' },
        { points: '+10%', label: 'Patients can buy' },
        { points: '+10%', label: 'Patients can grow' },
      ]}
    />

    <dl class="note">
      <dt><i style="background:var(--band-100)"></i>100%</dt>
      <dd>= full recreational access</dd>
      <dt><i style="background:var(--band-50)"></i>50%</dt>
      <dd>= best medical-only</dd>
      <dt><i style="background:var(--band-0)"></i>0%</dt>
      <dd>= fully illegal</dd>
    </dl>

    <h2>State X allows low-THC products, why is it a NO?</h2>
    <p>When states only allow low-THC cannabis, usually for medical use, they're still blocking it's true theraputic use. These laws are used to quell momentum, not to serve the public interest.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.5;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 30px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
  }
  h2 + p + p {
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  h2:nth-of-type(2) {
    margin-top: 36px;
  }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
    font-size: 0.9em;
    padding: 1px 5px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .or {
    color: var(--muted);
    text-align: center;
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-top: 22px;
  }
  .note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 8px 14px;
    align-items: center;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    border-radius: 14px;
    background: var(--card);
  }
  .note dt {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-weight: 800;
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
    color: var(--fg);
  }
  .note dt i {
    width: 12px;
    height: 12px;
    border-radius: 3px;
    flex: none;
  }
  .note dt:nth-of-type(2) i {
    box-shadow: var(--bar-inset);
  }
  .note dd {
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 1024px) {
    .about {
      max-width: 640px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 44px;
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }
    h2 {
      font-size: 24px;
    }
    .or {
      font-size: 15px;
    }
    .note {
      font-size: 16px;
    }
  }
</style>
